# Example 6: CRISPR-Cas gene editing
# Concept demo: sgRNA design -> Cas9 cleavage -> NHEJ/HDR repair
#
# This .helix file declares one editing operation via the #crispr bio-instruction annotation,
# with the target gene containing a readable ORF; the Python API comments below supplement with equivalent script calls.
#
# Target gene: DNA sequence containing an NGG PAM (SpCas9 recognition site)
# PAM = 5'-NGG-3', located downstream of the spacer

#gene name=target_gene
ATG GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

# CRISPR edit instruction: insert "GGGG" with SpCas9 at position=50 of target_gene
# The parser records it as BioInstruction(kind=crispr, target=target_gene, params=...)
#crispr target=target_gene position=50 new_sequence="GGGG" cas=SpCas9 repair=HDR

